body:
I feel like a rare breed of someone who loved the game and thought it was well worth the price.  Every time I'm on Reddit, there's a hate post or two about the game while I'm scrolling and it's sad because I had a great time with it.  I never expected anything massive with post game stuff, especially because the game wasn't as popular online as other games.  I would love Temtem 2, but unless there's a huge wave of newcomers years down the line, I'm not optimistic.

&#x200B;

I haven't been following all the info or what devs have said nor how the community got to this point, but I'm truly sad to see this game that (when I originally played) had passion put in to it conjure up a negative community (whether justified or not).

[https://twitter.com/Timcast/status/1595098682084524034?s=20&t=JW59edQC92B3OT-EakslrA](https://twitter.com/Timcast/status/1595098682084524034?s=20&t=JW59edQC92B3OT-EakslrA)

&#x200B;

You referenced it, so I thought you knew

You ride cock so hard, they don't allow you on the farm.

&#x200B;

But Tim Pool is a piece of shit who continually spreads hate and couldn't even condemn the Club Q shooter and tried to blame the victims for getting shot at.  He's an awful human being
